{"indicator":"pm25","unit":"μg/m³","years":[2010,2011,2012,2013,2014,2015,2016,2017,2018,2019,2020,2021,2022,2023],"notes":{"TWN":"台灣不在 WHO 資料庫中，改用環境部 PM2.5 手動監測站（30 個一般測站與陽明國家公園測站）年平均的算術平均，2015 年起（之前的開放資料只有 8 站；環境部公布的 2013 年是 24.0、2014 年是 23.6）。這是測站的簡單平均，不是 WHO 依衛星、模型與人口分布推估的人口加權平均。2023 年算出 13.8 μg/m³，環境部公布的全國平均是 13.7；地圖只到 2023 年，環境部公布的 2024 年是 12.8、2025 年是 12.8","HKG":"WHO 的 PM2.5 估計（SDG 11.6.2）沒有分開列出香港，所以地圖上留空。參考：WashU ACAG 的衛星推估 2023 年是 16.2 μg/m³，跟 WHO 是不同的模型，不能直接比；「超過 WHO 指引值的人口比例」有香港的值","MAC":"WHO 的 PM2.5 估計（SDG 11.6.2）沒有分開列出澳門，所以地圖上留空。參考：WashU ACAG 的衛星推估 2023 年是 18.0 μg/m³，跟 WHO 是不同的模型，不能直接比；「超過 WHO 指引值的人口比例」有澳門的值"},"notesEn":{"TWN":"Taiwan is not in the WHO database; the arithmetic mean of the annual averages at the Ministry of Environment's manual PM2.5 monitoring stations (30 general stations plus the Yangmingshan National Park station) is used instead, from 2015 (earlier open data cover only 8 stations; the Ministry's figures are 24.0 for 2013, 23.6 for 2014). This is a simple average of monitoring stations, not a population-weighted estimate from satellites, models and population distribution like WHO's. The 2023 figure calculated here is 13.8 μg/m³, against the Ministry's published national average of 13.7. The map ends in 2023; the Ministry's figures are 12.8 for 2024, 12.8 for 2025","HKG":"WHO's PM2.5 estimates (SDG 11.6.2) do not list Hong Kong separately, so it is left blank. For reference, WashU ACAG's satellite-based estimate for 2023 is 16.2 μg/m³, from a different model that is not directly comparable; “People above WHO guideline” does include Hong Kong","MAC":"WHO's PM2.5 estimates (SDG 11.6.2) do not list Macao separately, so it is left blank. For reference, WashU ACAG's satellite-based estimate for 2023 is 18.0 μg/m³, from a different model that is not directly comparable; “People above WHO guideline” does include Macao"},"encoding":"delta","aggregates":{"WLD":[-2,3439,-61,-2,9,-144,20,-92,-95,-157,-150,-231,33,-80,117]},"values":{"ABW":[-2,